## Phase 5 prototype: comments pinned on the board

On a PR's portal page (`/pr-N/`), the PCB and Schematic tabs get:

- a **Comment** mode: click a part (its position and reference) or any point of the board (camera `screen_to_world`), or type x/y, write the note;
- **posting** as a PR conversation comment through the REST API, ending in a hidden `kicad-hub-pin` marker and an `?at=x,y&ref=…#pcb` link back to the page. Fine-grained token (Pull requests: Read and write) in `localStorage`, "Forget token" button, sent only to `api.github.com`. Without a token the comment is copied and the PR opened;
- a **Comments** card in the side panel listing the pins found in the PR's comments (paginated, token optional); clicking one selects the part or zooms to the point and turns the board to the pin's side;
- numbered **markers drawn over the viewer**, repositioned when the camera changes.

Comment text is escaped everywhere (plain text, never HTML). Only PR pages of github.com repos. The feature lives in `scripts/pins.js` (copied to `assets/` by `portal.py index`); `portal.html` has two small hooks (load `pins.js`, announce the viewer) and `portal.py` embeds the PR number.

Not run in a browser by the author (no headless browsers allowed here): needs a manual test of posting, see the steps in the PR conversation. README ("Comments on the board", token steps) and ROADMAP (phase 5) updated.

